{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the leaders brought.</b> When Israel went up from Egypt, each man asked according to his stature. The two שהם stones, which were for the ephod — all the leaders brought together, because the names of all the tribes are written on them." "<b>And the setting stones.</b> Which were for the choshen — each one brought a single stone, to seal upon it the name of his tribe. And also the anointing oil they brought, for it is the holiest of all. And משחה is an expression of greatness, because with it they would anoint kings and the High Priest. And also the incense that was burned on the golden altar, and that which was burned in the innermost sanctuary."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:01.827812102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}